Also someone in my life had the argument that sqrt(2) can
not possibly but -2 because "two negatives will never make
a positive". I of course made a diagram : 




                                         |                                  

                                         | area = (+2) x (+2) = +4                               
                                      +2 +-----------------+                
                                         |                 |                
                                         |                 |                
                                         |                 |                
                                         |                 |                
                                      +1 +                 |                
                                         |                 |                
                                         |                 |                
                                         |                 |                
                                         |                 |                
                   ----+--------+--------+--------+--------+-----------
                      -2       -1        0       +1       +2
                       |                 |                                  
                       |                 |                                  
                       |                 |                                  
                       |                 |                                  
                       |              -1 +                                  
                       |                 |                                  
                       |                 |                                  
                       |                 |      two different things              
                       |                 |                 |                
                       +------------  -2 +               --+  +2 x (-2)
                                         |                                  
               area = (-2) x (-2) = +4   |      this is not (+2)^2
                                         |        nor is it (-2)^2                                  


                                                                  
Here we see the area of the square ( -2 )^2 is in fact positive 4. What
is a negative area anyways? To this I get the question "but see that a
-2 multiplied by -2 is the number -4 and not +4 so you must be wrong?"
I take a sip of whiskey, smile, and then say "that is not the square of
two things which are identical."  That got me no where. This is yet
another reason why I drink sometimes.

Dennis Clarke 

